hadiths[135]{hadithnumber,text}:
"608","'Abdu'r-Rahman ibn Yazid said"
"609","Abu Hurayra reported that the Messenger of Allah"
"610","Anas reported that the Messenger of Allah"
"611","Abu Nu'aym"
"612","'A'isha say that she saw the Prophet"
"613","Abu Hurayra said"
"614","Anas said"
"615","'Ikrima heard 'A'isha"
"616","Jabir ibn 'Abdullah reported that at-Tufayl ibn 'Amr asked the\nProphet"
"617","Anas ibn Malik said"
"618","Abu Hurayra reported that the Messenger of Allah"
"619","Shaddad ibn Aws reported that the Prophet"
"620","Ibn 'Umar said"
"621","'A'isha said"
"622","Similar to hadith 617 but with a slightly different wording."
"623","'Abdullah ibn 'Umar said"
"624","'Glory be to Allah';\n'Praise be to Allah'; and 'There is no god but Allah' a hundred times."
"625","'Abdullah ibn 'Amr reported that the Prophet"
"626","Abu Bakr as-Siddiq was heard to say"
"627","Safwan ibn 'Abdullah ibn Safwan"
"628","'Abdullah ibn 'Amr reported that a man said"
"629","Ibn 'Umar said"
"630","Ibn 'Umar said"
"631","It is reported that 'Umar used to make supplication with his words"
"632","'Our Lord"
"633","When Anas made supplication for his brother"
"634","'Amr ibn al-Harith said"
"635","Anas ibn Malik was told"
"636","Anas ibn Malik said"
"637","Anas reported that a woman came to the Prophet"
"638","The Prophet"
"639","A man came to the Prophet"
"640","'Glory be to Allah\nwho has no partner. His is the Kingdom and praise is His and He has power\nover all things. There is no power nor strength except by Allah. Glory be\nto Allah and by His praise."
"641","O Allah"
"642","Abu Sa'id al-Khudri reported that the Prophet"
"643","Abu Hurayra reported that the Prophet"
"644","Malik ibn Aws ibn al-Hadathan said"
"645","Anas ibn Malik reported that the Prophet"
"646","Jabir ibn 'Abdullah reported that the Prophet"
"647","Abu Hurayra reported that the Messenger of Allah"
"648","Similar to 644 except it has """"Shame on"""" rather than """"Wretched is;"""""
"649","'Glory be to Allah and by His praise in number as great as His creation\nand in accordance with His own pleasure and the weight of His Throne and\nthe extent of His words.'"
"650","Abu Hurayra reported that the Messenger of Allah"
"651","Jabir reported that the Messenger of Allah"
"652","Abu Hurayra reported that the Prophet"
"653","Tariq ibn Ashyam al-Ashja'i said"
"654","Umm Qays reported that the Prophet"
"655","Anas said"
"656","Abu Hurayra reported that the Messenger of Allah"
"657","Abu Hurayra reported that the Messenger of Allah"
"658","'Amr ibn Shu'ayb reported that his grandfather said"
"659","Abu Hurayra reported that the Prophet"
"660","Abu Hurayra reported that the Prophet"
"661","Anas reported that the Messenger of Allah"
"662","'Uthman said that he heard the Prophet"
"663","when the call to prayer has been given\nand when in battle ranks in the Cause of Allah."
"664","Abu Sirma reported that the Messenger of Allah"
"665","'O Allah"
"666","'Abdullah ibn 'Abbas reported that the Messenger of Allah may Allah\nbless him and grant him peace"
"667","'O Allah"
"668","Mu'awiya ibn Abi Sufyan said on the minbar"
"669","Abu Hurayra reported that the Prophet"
"670","'O Allah"
"671","Abu Hurayra reported that the Prophet"
"672","laziness"
"673","Anas ibn Malik said"
"674","Anas said"
"675","Abu Hurayra said"
"676","'Abdullah said"
"677","Thumana ibn Huzn said"
"678","'Abdullah ibn Abi 'Awfa reported that the Prophet"
"679","Anas reported that the Prophet"
"680","Abu Hurayra reported that the Prophet"
"681","O\nAllah"
"682","'Amr ibn Shu'ayb reported from his father that his grandfather said"
"683","Ibn 'Abbas used to say"
"684","Anas said"
"685","Anas said"
"686","'O Allah"
"687","'Abdullah ibn 'Umar said"
"688","'A'isha said"
"689","Isma'il ibn Qays said"
"690","Abu Musa reported that the Prophet"
"691","Abu Musa al-Ash'ari used to use this supplication"
"692","O Allah"
"693","Abu Ayyub al-Ansari said"
"694","Anas said"
"695","'A'isha said"
"696","'I seek refuge with You from the punishment of Hellfire"
"697","Ibn 'Abbas said"
"698","'Abdullah ibn 'Abbas said"
"699","'Abdullah ibn 'Abbas said """"When the Messenger of Allah"
"700","'O Allah"
"701","Rifa'a az-Zurqi said"
"702","'There is no\ngod but Allah"
"703","'O Allah"
"704","'There is no\ngod but Allah"
"705","Jabir said"
"706","Jabir ibn 'Abdullah said"
"707","Anas said"
"708","'Abdullah ibn 'Amr was heard to say"
"709","'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud said"
"710","Ibn 'Abbas said"
"711","'I\nask You by (the words) """"There is no god but You"
"712","either his supplication is answered quickly"
"713","Abu Hurayra reported that the Prophet"
"714","Abu Hurayra reported that the Prophet"
"715","Abu Hurayra reported that the Prophet"
"716","An-Nu'man ibn Bashir reported that the Prophet"
"717","'A'isha said"
"718","Maqil bin Yasar (ra) said that he came to the Prophet (ﷺ) with Abu Bakr (ra). He said"
"719","O Allah"
"720"," O Allah cause this wind to bring rain and let it not be without benefit""""."""""
"721","(O Allah! We ask you the good of this wind and the good of what is therein and the good with which it is sent.)"
"722","It is stated by sayidina Abu Hurayrah (ra) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said """"Wind is the mercy of Allah. It brings mercy or punishment. Do not denounce it but ask Allah"
"723","“O Allah"
"724","“Glory be to him whom you glorified.” He said that the thunderclap is an angel who yells at the rainclouds as a shepherd yells at his sheep/goats."
"725","“Glory be to him whose praise the thunderclap sings and the angels glorify in awe of him”. He used to say"
"726","Awsat bin Ismail has narrated that he heard Abu Bakr (ra) say after the death of the Prophet (ﷺ) “This is the very place where the Prophet (ﷺ)"
"727","“O Allah"
"728","Abbas bin Abdul Mmuttalib (ra) said that he requested the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) to teach him a supplication whereby he May request Allah for his needs. The Prophet (ﷺ) said"
"729","(O Allah"
"730","O Allah"
"731","(O Allah"
"732","Abu Hurayrah (ra) has narrated that the Prophet (ﷺ) sought refuge in Allah from the distress of trial"
"733","Abu Naufal bin Abu Aqrab has narrated on the authority of his father that he asked the Prophet (ﷺ) about (voluntary) fasts. He said"
"734","Jabir bin Abdullah (ra) said that they were with the Prophet (ﷺ)when a very stinking gush of wind blew over there. The Prophet (ﷺ) they asked his companions (ra) if they knew what that was. He added"
"735","Jabir (ra) said that (once) a bad smelling wind blew in the times of the prophet Ig. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said"
"736","It is reported by Qasim bin Abdur Rahman as-Shami that he heard Ibn Unm Abd say"
"737","It is reported by Jabir bin Abdullah (ra) that they had accompanied the messenger of Allah when they came to two graves. Both the inmate of the graves were being punished. He said"
"738","It is reported by Qays that Amr bin al-Aas (ra) was going somewhere with his friends. They saw a dead mule whose belly had swollen up. Amr (ra)said"
"739","It is reported by Abu Hurayrah (ra) that Maiz bin Maalik al-Aslami (ra) came to the Prophet (ﷺ) repeatedly (so that he may be given the prescribed punishment for the sin he had committed). When he came the fourth time"
"740","Ubadah bin Walid said that he came out with his father Ubadah bin al-Samit and he was a young man at that time. They met an elderly \nShaikh who had a mantle over him and Maafi garments. His slave too had a mantle and Maafai. The narrator (Ubadah bin Walid) said"
"741","Muhammad bin Ziyad said that he found that the predecessors (that is"
"742"," ... but give  preference over themselves"
